  "approved_payload": {
    "content": "Police say two armed men stormed a homestead in Komkhulu locality, Konkwana administrative area, near Willowvale, at about 18:45 on Tuesday 13 October, held five people at gunpoint and demanded cash and a firearm, then shot dead the headman, 44, and his mother, 70. His wife and two others were unhurt. The Provincial Serious and Violent Crime Investigation unit is on the case; no arrests reported. The Dispatch calls it the second killing of a traditional leader in Willowvale in about a month; no source links the two. The victims were not named.",
